# Trivy accepted-risk list. Every entry needs a reason, a date and an expiry (exp:YYYY-MM-DD);
# an expired entry stops applying and the dependency audit fails again.
#
# picomatch <= 4.0.7 ReDoS (GHSA-fc5q-39xc-vjpf), accepted 2026-11-17 by the owner: no fixed
# version exists, the package is dev tooling only (eslint, vite, vitest via tinyglobby) and is
# not in any image. Re-check: when picomatch publishes a fix, bump it and delete this entry,
# the pnpm auditConfig entry and the .grype.yaml rule.
CVE-2026-112366 exp:2026-12-17
#
# nginx 1.30.6-r1 in the frontend image (five High advisories, fixed in nginx 1.30.7), accepted
# 2026-11-18 by the owner until 2026-11-26: the pinned base image
# nginxinc/nginx-unprivileged:stable-alpine had not published 1.30.7 yet (the official
# nginx:stable-alpine had), and the base image pins nginx=1.30.6-r1 so `apk upgrade` cannot pull
# the fix. Which of the five apply to frontend/nginx.conf (a reverse proxy to the API) has not
# been assessed. Trivy ignores by advisory id, not by package. Re-check: when nginx-unprivileged
# 1.30.7 is published, bump the digest in frontend/Dockerfile and delete these five entries and
# the nginx-base rules and marker in .grype.yaml.
CVE-2026-113425 exp:2026-11-26
CVE-2026-121810 exp:2026-11-26
CVE-2026-123007 exp:2026-11-26
CVE-2026-123633 exp:2026-11-26
CVE-2026-123634 exp:2026-11-26
#
# CVE-2026-118899 (High, nginx 1.30.6-r1, fixed in 1.30.7): same package, cause and re-check
# trigger as the five above; accepted 2026-11-19 by the owner until the same date. Rechecked
# 2026-11-19: the newest nginx-unprivileged:stable-alpine digest still ships and pins
# nginx=1.30.6-r1. The advisory concerns a listen directive with the ssl parameter;
# frontend/nginx/templates/default.conf.template has only a plain listen 8080 (TLS ends at the
# platform ingress), so the affected listener is not configured in this image.
CVE-2026-118899 exp:2026-11-26
